{
  "requirement": "Under {cite}`requirements.cli.skill_structure`, the `habeas-evidence` skill MUST be the home of the authoring workflow, fixing validation findings, outcomes and FIXME judgments, citation and site reviews, disagreeing assessments, and the commit message for a change to agreed requirement text.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement says `habeas-evidence` MUST be the home of seven topics: the authoring workflow, fixing validation findings, outcomes and FIXME judgments, citation and site reviews, disagreeing assessments, and the commit message for a change to agreed requirement text. A skill is its `SKILL.md` plus its `references/` files. The parent `requirements.cli.skill_structure` says each topic is stated in full in exactly one skill.\n\nThe test is `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_evidence_skill_is_home_of_authoring_findings_and_assessment_outcomes]`. It covers each topic as follows:\n\n- **Authoring workflow:** `section(raw, \"## Workflow\")` of `SKILL.md` must contain `` `habeas author --all` ``.\n- **Fixing findings:** the `## Fixing findings` section must contain the `| Finding | Action |` table and the `### Missing test and example references` heading.\n- **Disagreeing assessments:** the `## Disagreeing assessments` section must contain \"The goal is\".\n- **Commit message:** the `## Rules` section must contain \"in the message of the commit that makes it\".\n- **FIXME judgments:** `references/fixme.md` must contain `# FIXME judgments`.\n- **Citation and site reviews:** `references/reviews.md` must contain both `## Citation reviews` and `## Site reviews`.\n- **Outcomes:** `assert_home(\"habeas-evidence\")` requires every marker from `home_markers` in the bundled evidence skill. These include \"A judgment is one of three outcomes\", the FIXME-judgment marker, the citation-review and site-review markers, \"The goal is that independent assessments…\" and the commit-message marker. The same call asserts that none of the other four skills contains any of those markers. That checks that these topics are stated in the evidence skill and not restated elsewhere.\n\nThe assertions are real: `assert_text` and `assert_home` panic on a missing phrase or on a restatement in another skill. The outcomes topic has no assertion in the test body. The helper `assert_home` covers it through the \"three outcomes\" marker.\n\nThe `SKILLS` list and `skill_files` define the skill's files, and `bundled_skills_are_five_skill_directories_each_home_to_its_topics` checks that this listing matches the files on disk. No topic named in the requirement lacks a test. The checks are phrase-based, which suits a requirement about where skill text lives. I found no gap.",
  "references": "705ed82e4b6db789bc1e43ba36e10077d3f5b824870ae00641b8c90ee5333b95",
